{
  "_comment": [
    "TEMPLATE for ~/.claude/settings.project.json, the settings file the `pj`",
    "launcher reads (home/.zshrc passes --settings at it).",
    "",
    "WHY A TEMPLATE AND NOT A STOWED FILE. The real file has to carry ABSOLUTE",
    "paths -- see below -- so a stowed copy would commit a username to a public",
    "repo, and the pre-commit leak gate blocks that, correctly. Rendering at",
    "install time keeps the repo username-free and still versions the content.",
    "Before 2026-09-19 this file was tracked by NOTHING: not this repo, not a stow",
    "symlink, not dot-claude. A rebuilt machine would have started pj bare.",
    "",
    "__HOME__ IS REPLACED WITH $HOME AT RENDER TIME by",
    "claude-project-settings-render, which install.sh runs.",
    "",
    "WHY NOT JUST WRITE ${HOME} AND LET CLAUDE CODE EXPAND IT. Because it does",
    "not. Measured 2026-09-19 against a live session's own process environment:",
    "the file said PROJECTS_DIR=${HOME}/CODE/CaptainCodeAU and the process",
    "received the LITERAL string ${HOME}/CODE/CaptainCodeAU. Anything reading that",
    "variable directly got a path that does not exist. It had been that way",
    "unnoticed because nothing checks an env var for plausibility.",
    "",
    "THE EXCEPTION IS A COMMAND STRING. statusLine.command runs through a shell,",
    "so its \"$HOME\" expands properly and is deliberately NOT templated. The rule:",
    "$HOME works where a shell will see it, never in an env value or a path list.",
    "",
    "NO hooks KEY HERE, EVER. Hooks are declared once in settings/claude/hooks.json",
    "and registered by claude-hooks-sync --target project. The renderer MERGES any",
    "existing hooks back before it writes, so a re-render cannot drop them -- but a",
    "hooks key in this template would fight that mechanism and win silently.",
    "",
    "WHY verbose IS HERE. --setting-sources project,local means ~/.claude/settings.json",
    "is never read, so every key it holds is dropped unless this file restores it.",
    "verbose:true lives there, and its absence is why a pj footer shows no token count",
    "while a `c` footer does. Proven 2026-09-20 in one throwaway pane, same alias, one",
    "flag changed: `pj --verbose` rendered \"0 tokens\", plain `pj` rendered it nowhere",
    "in any of the pane's 19 content rows. The indicators are a STACK, not a list, so",
    "the missing slot closes up and \"high · /effort\" moves up a row -- which is why",
    "this read as a DIFFERENT item rather than a missing one.",
    "",
    "THE AUDIT IS DONE. F5b, 2026-09-21, settled every remaining key at a gate:",
    "47 were still dropped (not 48 -- a recount, the number in a record about a",
    "growing thing goes stale the day it is written). 10 restored below, 3 became",
    "PROFILE keys, 34 stay dropped with a reason recorded on W-20260920-A03.",
    "Restoring them one at a time was the failure mode; the audit replaced it.",
    "",
    "Top-level keys beginning with _ are stripped at render time; this note is one."
  ],
  "_five_settings_layers": [
    "THE FIVE SETTINGS LAYERS, and which file each one is under pj (W-20260922-A10).",
    "Measured 2026-09-22 in F8a with $.settings.read({source}) and cross-checked against",
    "every file on disk. Written here so a settings audit reads it instead of re-deriving it.",
    "",
    "  policy   managed settings: /Library/Application Support/ClaudeCode/managed-settings.json",
    "           EMPTY on this machine (0 keys). Reaches every launcher, every config dir,",
    "           and survives --safe-mode; --setting-sources cannot exclude it (F5b Part C).",
    "  user     <config_dir>/settings.json. Under pj this is NOT READ: pj passes",
    "           --setting-sources project,local. Under a profile it is that profile's dir",
    "           (~/.claude-scratch/settings.json), never ~/.claude/settings.json.",
    "  project  the repo's .claude/settings.json (hooks, mostly).",
    "  local    the repo's .claude/settings.local.json (permissions, sandbox).",
    "  flag     THIS FILE, rendered to ~/.claude/settings.project.json and passed with",
    "           --settings. pj's own settings are the FLAG layer, not user or project.",
    "",
    "Later layers win per key. A second --settings (the profile overlay for remote_control",
    "and voice) merges on top of this file rather than replacing it (F5b, three arms)."
  ],
  "cleanupPeriodDays": 1825,
  "claudeMdExcludes": [
    "__HOME__/.claude/CLAUDE.md"
  ],
  "_theme_why": [
    "W-20260920-A03, restored at the P8b gate 2026-09-21. `pj` passes",
    "--setting-sources project,local, so ~/.claude/settings.json is never read and",
    "all 61 of its top-level keys are dropped; this file restores them by hand and",
    "restores 13 of the 61. The other 48 are preferences and costs and are a",
    "decision PER KEY, deferred to F5 -- do not restore that list wholesale, several",
    "are dropped on purpose.",
    "",
    "THIS ONE IS NOT A PREFERENCE. `dark-daltonized` is a colour-vision",
    "accessibility setting, and it was silently off in the launcher used most.",
    "Absence in a UI looks exactly like a deliberate default, which is why it sat",
    "unnoticed: nothing was broken, the colours were just wrong for the person",
    "reading them. Accessibility does not wait for a stage.",
    "",
    "Same mechanism as the SessionStart hooks that never registered, the literal",
    "${HOME} env values, and the dropped verbose:true -- fourth instance."
  ],
  "theme": "dark-daltonized",
  "_f8a_attribution_why": [
    "EMPTY ON PURPOSE -- DO NOT RESTORE (D-20260922-A07, ruled at the F8a gate).",
    "",
    "Empty strings mean Claude Code composes NO attribution text for a commit or",
    "a PR. `_audit-chain`'s five C-* trailers ARE the attribution here, and the",
    "engine's own line would duplicate them. Those trailers are stamped",
    "unconditionally by the prepare-commit-msg hook on the global core.hooksPath,",
    "so they also cover commits a SCRIPT makes inside a session (open-items,",
    "pj-wrap). An engine attribution line is text the MODEL is told to write, so",
    "it can be reworded, dropped, or never written on a script commit.",
    "",
    "This key had no comment until 2026-09-22 and nothing recorded the reason:",
    "`decided` returned a clean miss and F4's report mentions the word only as a",
    "filename. F8a then hooked `attribution.text` and the event never fired,",
    "which reads exactly like a dead event until you find this key. It is not",
    "dead: restoring attribution through a one-off --settings overlay made it",
    "fire four times and a probe mod's trailer land in the commit message."
  ],
