  "_f5b_hook_security_why": [
    "W-20260920-A03, F5b 2026-09-21. THE TWO KEYS BELOW ARE THE REAL FINDING OF",
    "THE AUDIT, and neither was dropped on purpose -- both were lost by accident",
    "when pj stopped reading ~/.claude/settings.json.",
    "",
    "Both are RESTRICTIONS whose ABSENCE means NO RESTRICTION. From the schema,",
    "quoted: allowedHttpHookUrls -- 'When set, hooks with non-matching URLs are",
    "blocked. Undefined = no restriction, empty array = block all HTTP hooks.'",
    "httpHookAllowedEnvVars -- 'each hook's effective allowedEnvVars is the",
    "intersection with this list. Undefined = no restriction.'",
    "",
    "So `c` limited HTTP hooks to localhost:31337 and blocked every environment",
    "variable from reaching a hook header, while `pj` -- the launcher that runs",
    "with --dangerously-skip-permissions -- had NO limit on either. The less",
    "guarded launcher was the one with fewer guard rails, which is backwards.",
    "",
    "This is the same shape as the missing SessionStart hooks and the dropped",
    "verbose: an absent restriction and a deliberate default look identical, and",
    "a security setting that is silently off looks exactly like one that is on."
  ],
  "allowedHttpHookUrls": [
    "http://localhost:31337/hooks/*"
  ],
  "httpHookAllowedEnvVars": [],

  "_f5b_a11y_and_input_why": [
    "tui:'default' is the classic main-screen renderer. It is the settings-key",
    "sibling of CLAUDE_CODE_DISABLE_ALTERNATE_SCREEN=1, which memory records as",
    "forced for accessibility with 'don't remove'. Same class as theme above:",
    "an accessibility setting that was silently off in the launcher used most.",
    "",
    "leftArrowOpensAgents:false -- measured live 2026-09-21, a pj session's",
    "footer reads 'left-arrow for agents' and a `c` session's does not. A real",
    "behaviour difference, chosen once and then quietly reverted by the launcher."
  ],
  "tui": "default",
  "leftArrowOpensAgents": false,

  "_f5b_notifications_why": [
    "awaySummaryEnabled -- the schema default is TRUE, so pj was SHOWING a",
    "session recap that `c` does not. Dropping a false is not a no-op: it turns",
    "the feature ON. That is the trap this whole item is about.",
    "",
    "preferredNotifChannel -- where task-complete and permission pings go.",
    "CAVEAT, stated because it is unverified: the docs list only auto,",
    "terminal_bell and notifications_disabled. 'iterm2_with_bell' is the live",
    "value from ~/.claude/settings.json and may be a legacy spelling. It is",
    "restored as-is to match `c`; if pings stop working, this line is the suspect."
  ],
  "awaySummaryEnabled": false,
  "preferredNotifChannel": "iterm2_with_bell",

  "_f5b_behaviour_why": [
    "autoMemoryEnabled -- RULING COMPLIANCE, not a preference. The schema default",
    "is TRUE, so every pj session has been running with Claude auto memory ON and",
    "writing to projects/<key>/memory/, against D-20260919-A07 which ruled that",
    "the Claude memory stores stay off and MEMORY.md is the store. The ruling was",
    "made, and the launcher quietly broke it, because the key lived in the file",
    "pj does not read.",
    "",
    "plansDirectory -- the default is ~/.claude/plans. This repo keeps its specs",
    "in Plans/ and memory tracks them there, so a pj session entering plan mode",
    "was writing plans where nobody looks.",
    "",
    "respondToBashCommands:false -- a `! command` adds its output to context",
    "without Claude replying.",
    "",
    "skillListingBudgetFraction -- 1.5% of context for the skill listing instead",
    "of the 1% default, matching `c`.",
    "",
    "DELIBERATELY NOT HERE: autoCompactEnabled. Ruled at the F5b gate that it",
    "STAYS DROPPED, so pj keeps auto-compact ON. Gavin's reason, recorded in his",
    "words: pj stage sessions run unattended for hours, and with auto-compact off",
    "a full context halts the session with nobody present to /compact. Under `c` a",
    "human is at the keyboard. A profile may set it off later for interactive use;",
    "the template keeps the default. Do not 'fix' this."
  ],
  "autoMemoryEnabled": false,
  "plansDirectory": "Plans/",
  "respondToBashCommands": false,
  "skillListingBudgetFraction": 0.015,
  "_f5c_sandbox_why": [
    "sandbox.excludedCommands -- the four pj tools that write outside the Bash",
    "sandbox's writable set, so they stop failing in a way that reads as something",
    "else. This lives HERE, in the pj-owned template, rather than in one repo's",
    ".claude/settings.local.json, because the drawer stalls happen in EVERY",
    "project. Ruled by Gavin at the F5c gate, 2026-09-22.",
    "",
    "THE PATTERN SYNTAX, measured 2026-09-22 against Claude Code 2.1.278, because",
    "every plausible reading of it is wrong in a different way:",
    "  - the pattern is matched against the WHOLE COMMAND, not the program name.",
    "    `touch` does NOT match `touch /path/file`. This is why the",
    "    excludedCommands:[\"git\"] that sat in .claude/settings.local.json from",
    "    before this stage had never once taken effect.",
    "  - `*` does NOT cross a `/`. `touch *` is denied for `touch /path/file`,",
    "    while `touch /path/*` matches it.",
    "  - `**` does cross `/` and is greedy to the end, so token count does not",
    "    matter: `touch **` matches a one-argument and a two-argument touch alike.",
    "  - a COMPOUND command escapes only if EVERY sub-command matches. One half",
    "    matching and the other not is denied ENTIRELY, including the half that",
    "    matched. That is the property that makes a trailing ** safe to write.",
    "",
    "GIT CANNOT BE EXCLUDED AND IS DELIBERATELY ABSENT. Gavin asked for",
    "`git -C ~/.claude **` at the gate. Measured and it does not work, by any",
    "spelling: `git **`, the absolute-path form, a token-for-token form, and even",
    "a bare `**` were ALL still sandboxed, and so was `env git ...` under `env **`.",
    "The controls separate: `touch **` exempts freely in the same folder in the",
    "same minute, a `git` token in the MIDDLE of a touch command does not spoil it,",
    "and the identical git command succeeds with the sandbox lifted. So Claude Code",
    "refuses to exempt git specifically. Writing dot-claude from a pj session still",
    "needs a per-command sandbox lift; do not re-add a git line here expecting it to",
    "work, and do not read its absence as an oversight.",
    "",
    "WHAT THIS COSTS, stated because it is a real trade and it was named at the",
    "gate: an excluded command runs UNSANDBOXED every time it matches, and",
    "open-items and decided are stowed from fifty-shades-of-dotfiles, so their",
    "SOURCE is writable from the working directory of any session standing in that",
    "repo. A session that edits those scripts is then editing something that runs",
    "outside the sandbox. They are here anyway because the alternative measured",
    "worse: open-items span for 60 seconds and then blamed a pid for a lock that",
    "did not exist (W-20260921-A44), and decided add hung until it was killed by",
    "hand (W-20260921-A30). Both were fixed to REFUSE rather than lie, which is the",
    "floor; this removes the refusal itself.",
    "",
    "The bare forms sit beside the ** forms because a bare pattern matches only the",
    "bare command: `open-items` alone and `open-items add ...` are two matches.",
    "",
    "pj-ping and pj-ping ** added 2026-09-23 (Gavin, D-20260921-A10 ping policy): every",
    "session signals with pj-ping, which plays afplay, sends imsg and writes its log under",
    "~/.local/state; all three fail inside the sandbox, so pj-ping runs outside it."
  ],
  "sandbox": {
    "excludedCommands": [
      "open-items",
      "open-items **",
      "decided",
      "decided **",
      "imsg **",
      "afplay **",
      "pj-ping",
      "pj-ping **"
    ]
  }
